      "message": "The pointer walks look right to me. As far as I can see, though, this is a generic fix rather than a P3S one: GKI builds with `CONFIG_UBSAN` (so `CONFIG_UBSAN_BOUNDS`), `CONFIG_UBSAN_TRAP` and `-fstrict-flex-arrays\u003d3`, so `swapon()` of a block device whose header lists two or more bad pages traps in `setup_swap_map()` today, with or without P3S.\n\nAs I asked on aosp/4368002, would one generic patch that declares `badpages[]` as a flexible array in `union swap_header` work for you instead? It would cover these three loops and `p3s_convert_swap_header()` without new locals.\n\nEither way, could the fix move out of the P3S series, ideally sent upstream and picked as `FROMLIST:`, or as `ANDROID: mm: swap: ...` otherwise?",
